        "topic": "Accounting Equation",
        "question_type": "Objective",
        "exam_year": "2016",
        "question_text": "<p>If assets are $15,000 and liabilities are $7,000, what is the owner's equity?</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>The accounting equation is: <b>Assets = Liabilities + Owner's Equity</b>. Rearranged, <b>Owner's Equity = Assets - Liabilities</b>. Thus, $15,000 - $7,000 = $8,000.</p>",
